mo Read the docs MULTI-STEP API CHECKS Chain the calls.  Assert at every step. A single GET proves a route exists. A sequence tests the contract: authenticate, create, read back, clean up. Name the request steps and assert their responses in your test; inspect the test outcome and recorded run evidence when it fails. Model the flow your integrators run: token, create, fetch, delete. Write assertions at each request and give the steps meaningful names. Review the test outcome and recorded runner evidence to identify the failed condition. Upload it the same way as a browser check: the files and an entry file. No browser, so every plan includes 10× as many API runs as browser runs. Same alerts and same run history as browser checks. Read about multi-step API checks Authenticate POST /oauth/token Create invoice POST /v1/invoices Read invoice GET /v1/invoices/:id Clean up DELETE /v1/invoices/:id Sample invoice-roundtrip · 200 → 201 → 200 → 204 · 837 ms total invoice-roundtrip Passed 5 min interval, us-east. 1 POST /oauth/token 200 212 ms · 2 POST /v1/invoices 201 388 ms · assert body.status == "draft" · 3 GET /v1/invoices/inv_2KxQ9 200 141 ms · assert body.total == 4900 · 4 DELETE /v1/invoices/inv_2KxQ9 204 96 ms. Total 837 ms. Same check Failed at step 3 404. assert body.total == 4900 not evaluated. WHERE IT RUNS Pick one region.  Or all four. Checks run from us-east, us-west, eu-west and ap-south, and all four are on every plan. Choose regions per monitor. One run = one execution in one region. Two regions = two runs per schedule. Region results sit side by side, so "fails in eu-west and ap-south only" is one glance. Each region's traffic leaves from one fixed IP. We share the list on request, so you can allowlist it. Every run executes in its own gVisor sandbox. Internal networks, cloud metadata and other sandboxes are unreachable from it. Estimate your runs eu-west Failed step 7 · 03:17 UTC ap-south Failed step 7 · 03:17 UTC us-east Passed 03:17 UTC us-west Passed 03