ep API checks on a schedule. A check runs your own @playwright/test spec, or a sequence of HTTP requests with assertions, and records the result. Synthetics overview CHECK TYPES Two. Browser (Playwright) and multi-step API. HTTP, DNS, TCP, ping, heartbeat and MCP server checks are part of uptime monitoring and do not use synthetic runs. Browser checks, Multi-step API checks RUNNER Playwright 1.62.1, one sandbox per run. Each run executes in its own gVisor sandbox with a read-only root filesystem. Egress is limited to public HTTP, HTTPS and DNS. How runs execute WHERE IT RUNS 4 regions. us-east, us-west, eu-west, ap-south. One execution in one region is one run. Each region's traffic leaves from one fixed IP, shared on request. Regions HOW SPECS GET IN Upload through the package API. Upload the spec and its files, name the entry spec, and set secrets. Secrets reach the spec as process.env.NAME and are masked in network logs, HAR, console and runner logs. Uploading a spec EVIDENCE Kept 14 days on every plan. Screenshot, video, Playwright trace, network log (HAR) and console for every failed run. Run evidence ALERTS 20 integrations on every plan, Free included. Email, Slack, Discord, Microsoft Teams, Webhook, PagerDuty, Opsgenie, Telegram, Google Chat, Pushover, Mattermost, Splunk On-Call, Pushbullet, Linear, incident.io, Rootly, Zapier, Datadog, Jira, GitLab. A failed run opens an incident. Alert channels WHAT IT IS NOT Not RUM, not load testing, not inside your network. It does not observe real visitors, does not generate load, and runs from DevHelm's 4 regions. What Synthetics is not Read the Synthetics docs FIT CHECK Is Synthetics right for your team?  Built for small SaaS teams with a handful of journeys that must not break. Strong fit when You have 3 to 30 engineers, customer-facing flows (signup, login, checkout, an API integrators call) and nobody whose full-time job is SRE. You already write, or can write, Playwright specs, and want them running outside CI. You depend on Stripe, Auth0 or an email provider and want to know when the flow breaks, not only when a vendor posts an incident. Not the best fit when You need checks to run from inside your private network. Checks run from DevHelm's 4 regions. You need load testing or real-user monitoring. This runs scripted checks, not traffic. You need a contractual SLA on the monitoring itself today. Book a demo Or apply to the design-partner program FAQ Frequently asked questions  Specs, runs, regions and access. The docs have the rest. What is the difference between synthetic monitoring and uptime monitoring? + Uptime monitoring checks that an endpoint responds. Synthetic monitoring runs a scripted user journey or API sequence and checks that it completes with the right result. DevHelm has both: uptime checks (HTTP, DNS, TCP, ping, heartbeat, MCP server) and Synthetics for Playwright and multi-step API checks. Do I have to rewrite my Playwright tests? + No. Upload the spec you already run, with the files it imports, and name the entry spec. Secrets reach it as process.env.NAME. Specs that depend on local-only state (a seeded database, a mocked server) need a production-safe version. What counts as a run, and what happens at my limit? + One execution in one region is one run, so two regions means two runs per schedule. Browser and API runs have separate monthly pools, and the usage meter shows where you are. When the included runs are used, new runs stop. No overage bill. How often can checks run? + Free every 60 minutes, Starter every 10, Pro every 5, Team every minute, Business every 30 seconds, Enterprise every 10 seconds. Shorter intervals use more runs; the calculator above shows how many. How do you handle flaky tests? + Turn on immediate retry: 0 to 10 attempts, off by default. When a spec fails on your app, DevHelm reruns it right away in the same region before deciding. A pass on retry is recorded as passed on retry; a repeat failure opens an incident. Retries count as runs. Where do checks run, and can I allowlist your IPs? + From us-east, us-west, eu-west and ap-south. Each region's traffic leaves from one fixed IP. We share the list on request. Can I monitor staging or something behind a firewall? + Staging works if it is reachable from the public internet on HTTP or HTTPS, for example behind basic auth or a token header. Anything reachable only inside your network can't be monitored today. Is it production ready? What does "beta" mean here? + It's in beta. Runs, evidence and alerts work today; run limits and regions can still change, and we announce changes in the changelog first. What is the AI SRE agent? + An investigation agent that starts from a failed run or check and reports whether it is your code or a vendor, with the evidence. It is available to design partners, installed and tuned by the DevHelm team. It is not self-serve and it does not change anything on its own. Read the docs Watch the flow,  not the homepage Access is by invitation. Book a 30-minute demo and we'll set up your workspace. Book a demo Read the docs Product Synthetics Webhook Testing Email Testing Build with DevHelm Developers Design partners Contact Company Security Privacy Terms DevHelm .io All systems operational © 2026 DevHelm.io Your homepage is up. Your checkout is not. — DevHelm

